# Build output and dependencies: reproduced by `npm ci` / `cargo build`.
node_modules/
dist/
target/

# Generated caches.
coverage/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# Evidence logs are deliverables, not build noise: `evidence/README.md`
# describes every one of them and `check:evidence-ledger` fails if a described
# artefact is missing. Without this re-include, a clean clone has no logs, so the
# ledger check passes locally (files on disk) and fails on the CI runner (files
# absent) - the exact class of defect that only a fresh checkout exposes.
!evidence/**/*.log

# External specification attachments. These are the two reference documents the
# redesign was measured against, kept locally for the audit trail. They are not
# product copy: `check:dashes`, `check:emoji`, and gitleaks all skip them on
# purpose, because they are someone else's text quoted as a requirement. They do
# not belong in the published tree.
[[]EK-A]*.txt
[[]EK-B]*.txt

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local secrets. The signing certificate and the updater private key never
# enter the tree (08-02 section 5); a build machine supplies them by path.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vendored binaries. `resources/manifest.json` pins every asset by SHA-256 and
# `resources/README.md` records its source, but the files themselves are
# fetched, not committed: the WebView2 evergreen installer alone is 215 MB,
# which exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, and the whole set is 307 MB of
# bytes that no line of code reads. `node resources/fetch.mjs` downloads each
# one and refuses a file whose hash does not match the manifest.
resources/toolchain/*.exe
resources/toolchain/*.zip
resources/installers/*.exe
resources/installers/*.zip
resources/fonts/*.zip
